---
// One proved theorem (/science/prove2me/theorems/<leaf>/): a leaf prove2me accepted a proof of, with its own share card
// (theorems/<leaf>/og.png) and JSON (theorems/<leaf>.json). Built for every accepted leaf the build's records hold
// (prove2me-theorems-build.ts); the browser refreshes its facts and its tasks from the gateway's records every minute.
// The statement itself is on prove2me until this page has a plain-English one. "The tasks": the leaf's tasks in the
// trial that proved it and who served each (prove2me-proof.ts).
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import type { GetStaticPaths } from 'astro';
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { p2m } from '../../../../data/prove2me';
import { day } from '../../../../data/prove2me-current';
import { THEOREMS_PATH, ctaHTML, gpuH, headTitle, nameOf, shortName, theoremFactsHTML, theoremPath, theoremReuseHTML, updatedText, type TheoremRow } from '../../../../data/prove2me-theorems';
import { buildTheorems } from '../../../../data/prove2me-theorems-build';
import { builtDetail, type TrialDetail } from '../../../../data/prove2me-records';
import { proofLeaf, proofTasksHTML } from '../../../../data/prove2me-proof';
import '../../../../styles/theorems.css';

export const getStaticPaths = (async () => (await buildTheorems()).pages.map((t) => ({ params: { leaf: t.leaf }, props: { t } }))) satisfies GetStaticPaths;

const { t } = Astro.props as { t: TheoremRow };
const { history, records, view, from, pages } = await buildTheorems();
const name = nameOf(t);
const at = t.verdict_at ?? t.submitted_at;
const reuse = t.kind === 'reuse';
// The leaf's tasks in the trial that proved it, as the prove2me page's list of that trial has them (prove2me-proof.ts):
// the gateway's campaign from trial 6 on, the build's data before; none for a reuse (no run).
const built = [builtDetail(p2m, history, t.trial)].filter((d): d is TrialDetail => !!d);
const proof = reuse ? null : proofLeaf(history, records, built, t);
const known = { history, pages: pages.map((x) => x.leaf), leaf: t.leaf };
const image = new URL(`${theoremPath(t.leaf)}og.png`, Astro.site).href;
const short = shortName(t);
const imageAlt = reuse
	? `${short}: closed by reuse on prove2me, ${day(at)}.`
	: `${short}: proved by ${p2m.model}, accepted by prove2me on ${day(at)}, ${gpuH(t.hours)} GPU-hours.`;
const description = reuse
	? `prove2me leaf ${t.leaf} (${short}), closed on ${day(at)} by reusing a theorem another prove2me user had proved; not counted as a proof by ${p2m.model}.`
	: `prove2me leaf ${t.leaf} (${short}): ${p2m.model}, an open model on the AIs@home network, proved it in trial ${t.trial} with ${gpuH(t.hours)} GPU-hours, and prove2me accepted the proof on ${day(at)}.`;
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: name,
		head: [
			// escaped: Starlight writes a head entry's content as raw HTML (headTitle)
			{ tag: 'title', content: headTitle(t) },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { property: 'og:image', content: image } },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { property: 'og:image:alt', content: imageAlt } },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { name: 'twitter:image:alt', content: imageAlt } },
		],
		description,
	}}
	headings={[
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'statement', text: 'Statement' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'proof', text: 'The proof' },
		...(reuse ? [] : [{ depth: 2, slug: 'tasks', text: 'The tasks' }]),
	]}
>
	<p class="th-kicker">{reuse ? 'Closed by reuse' : 'Accepted by prove2me'} · {day(at)}</p>
	<aside class="th-cta not-content" data-th-cta data-source="build" set:html={ctaHTML(t)} />
	<p class="th-updated" data-th-updated data-source="build">{updatedText(view, from === 'snapshot' ? 'saved' : 'build')}</p>
	<script is:inline type="application/json" data-th-known set:html={JSON.stringify(known).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />

	<h2 id="statement">Statement</h2>
	<div class="th-statement not-content">
		<p>
			<code>{t.theorem}</code>
		</p>
		<p>
			A plain-English statement is not written yet.{' '}
			{t.url ? <a href={t.url} data-statement>Statement on prove2me →</a> : 'The statement is on prove2me.'}
		</p>
	</div>
	<p>
		This is a leaf of prove2me: one piece of a theorem from a research paper, stated in Lean 4 by a prove2me user, not by AIs@home. It
		is one step toward the paper’s result, not the result itself.
	</p>

	<h2 id="proof">The proof</h2>
	{
		reuse ? (
			<p>
				This leaf was closed by reuse: the accepted proof is a theorem someone else had already proved on prove2me. We submitted the
				proof that uses it; it is not counted as a proof by {p2m.model}, nor in the costs. The proof <span data-reuses set:html={theoremReuseHTML(t)} />.
			</p>
		) : (
			<p>
				{p2m.model}, an open-weight model on the AIs@home network, wrote the proof as an agent in trial {t.trial}. Our own full check
				passed it (it builds, states exactly the leaf’s theorem, and uses no <code>sorry</code> and no axiom beyond Lean’s standard
				three), and prove2me’s check accepted it.
			</p>
		)
	}
	<dl class="th-facts not-content" data-th-facts data-source="build" set:html={theoremFactsHTML(t)} />
	<p class="th-note">
		GPU-hours and tokens are those of the leaf’s own tasks in the trial that proved it: the time the model spent generating, on one GPU.
		What a proof costs across all trials, failed leaves included, is on the <a href={THEOREMS_PATH + '#cost'}>list of proved theorems</a>.
	</p>
	{
		!reuse && (
			<Fragment>
				<h2 id="tasks">The tasks</h2>
				<p>
					The leaf’s tasks in trial {t.trial}: each outline the model wrote, a task for each hole the outline left, and the assembly
					that put the proof together, with what became of each, and which GPU did the model’s work. A GPU is named by its owner’s
					public username, the same one the <a href="/network/#board-title">leaderboard</a> shows; one without is named only by the kind of
					GPU it is.
				</p>
				<div class="th-tasks not-content" data-th-tasks data-source="build" set:html={proofTasksHTML(proof, false)} />
				{!proof && (
					<p class="th-note" data-th-tasks-none>
						Trial {t.trial} kept no per-task records; its run is on the <a href={`/science/prove2me/#trial-${t.trial}`}>prove2me page</a>.
					</p>
				)}
			</Fragment>
		)
	}
	<ul>
		<li><a href={THEOREMS_PATH}>Every proved theorem</a></li>
		<li><a href={`/science/prove2me/#trial-${t.trial}`}>Trial {t.trial} on the prove2me page</a>, with this leaf’s outlines and tasks</li>
		<li>This leaf as JSON: <a href={`${THEOREMS_PATH}${t.leaf}.json`}><code>{THEOREMS_PATH}{t.leaf}.json</code></a></li>
	</ul>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
	import { liveTheorems } from '../../../../scripts/theorems-live';
	liveTheorems();
</script>
